Summary:

A self-contained challenge: the target influencer TechReviewer2024 has profiles on three simulated platforms hosted inside the lab — ChirpNet (X-style microblog), ConnectPro (LinkedIn-style), and ForumHub (Reddit-style). All data lives in the instance, so the work is manual browsing and correlation, not external tooling. Reusing one identity across platforms lets you pivot from a professional profile to a real name, then to a covert negative-review campaign and its coordinated bot accounts.

Approach:

Work the platforms in order of structured-identity value:
ConnectPro first — the most structured identity data (name, employer, education).
ForumHub next — operational detail (moderator role, campaign thread, internal codename).
ChirpNet last — behavioral signals (follower account-creation timing).
Correlate shared data points across all three: the reused username ties the professional profile, the forum activity, and the microblog together.

